[73.850, "o", "\r\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n  mlassure Assessment Report\r\n  Target: churn-predictor-v1 (churn-predictor-endpoint)\r\n  Run at: 2026-06-10T11:26:42.873Z\r\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n  ✗ SI-6(1)      not-satisfied          conf:high    evidence:3\r\n      gap: No ModelQuality monitor schedule exists — only DataQuality is configured, meaning model performance metrics (e.g., accuracy, F1) are not monitored against a ground-truth baseline.\r\n      gap: Human attestation would be needed to confirm whether data capture was intentionally disabled for a maintenance window or is a persistent misconfiguration.\r\n      gap: No evidence of an alte"]
[0.000, "o", "rnative monitoring mechanism (e.g., external observability tooling) that could compensate for the disabled SageMaker data capture.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  ✗ AC-6(9)      not-satisfied          conf:high    evidence:1\r\n      gap: No resource-level tagging or SCP (Service Control Policy) evidence was available that might further restrict these overly broad IAM policies at the organization level — however, the IAM policies themselves are sufficient to determine non-conformance regardless.\r\n  ~ AU-12(3)     partially-satisfied    conf:high    evidence:3\r\n      gap: No registry entry or approval event found for the hotfix model package config 'churn-predictor-v1-hotfix' deployed on 2026-03-15. A human reviewer should confirm whether an out-of-band approval process (e.g., emergency change ticket) was followed for this hotfix, and whether a corresponding model package version exists in a separate registry group.\r\n      gap: Only one model package version (v1) is present in the registry. If additional versions were created for the hotfix, they may reside in a different model package group not captured by the current collector.\r\n  ✗ SC-28        not-satisfied   "]
